            "review_text": "geoffthompson383\nTien Giang Province, Vietnam4 contributions\n0\nThis place is amazing!!!\nAug 2017 • Family\nI am beyond impressed with their soups. This little joint is your definition of mom and pop/hole in the wall eatery. But the food is . I ordered the Shrimp spring rolls (generic but no complaints), bun bo hue and xl pho with meatballs and raw beef. The color of the bun bo hue broth was bright in red and glistening of a delicious oily hue. I could smell the fragrant lemongrass and aroma of a variety of spices. One gulp of the broth and i was taken. Sometimes broths can be too salty, or too sweet, or neither. This broth was exactly right. No extras were necessary. A few dallops of their crushed fresh chilis in my bowl was all it needed. The oho broth was just as amazing. It didn't leave the taste buds desiring more. Overall, I am a happy customer. It will always remain on my go to when in Hawaii.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 25, 2017",
